; Tessera stdlib: F128 transcendental functions
;
; exp and log for F128 are computed in Wide, a 192-bit-mantissa float, then
; rounded once to F128. The 79 bits beyond F128's 113 absorb the rounding of
; every intermediate step (each at most 2^-190 relative) and the truncation of
; the series, so the results are faithful: within 1 ulp, and almost always the
; correctly rounded value. The method follows RazorForge's B128Math and TLFloat
; (Naoki Shibata, Boost 1.0); the series coefficients and constants below were
; computed to 192 bits with exact rationals and mpmath.

; A finite float mant × 2^(exp - 191) with the mantissa's top bit (191) set;
; zero has a zero mantissa. The mantissa is hi (bits 191..64) and lo (63..0).
record Wide
    negative: Bool
    exp:      I64
    hi:       I128
    lo:       I64

